  "tacticalAnalysis": {
    "EGY": "Egypt's 4-2-3-1 focused on possession control (53.7%), building through the midfield pair of FATOUH and LASHIN who combined for 147 passes. An early SABER goal at min 4 from a deflected loose ball gave them the lead, but Egypt generated only 0.92 xG from 15 shots — poor conversion of chances. Defensively EGY operated in a mid/low block (23 mid + 15 low block phases), conceding just 5 defensive line breaks all match, but IRN's 2.24 xG exposed vulnerability when the press was bypassed. Egypt lacked incisive attacking combinations to break down IRN's 5-4-1.",
    "IRN": "IR Iran's compact 5-4-1 sat deep (30 low block phases, 26 mid block), generating the match's highest xG (2.24) through wing-back aggression and transition. TAREMI's missed penalty at min 10 was a pivotal miss, but the team responded immediately — MOHAMMADI forced a save at 13' and REZAEIAN scored the rebound. IRN pressed with high volume (278 pressures, 45 direct) despite only 36.4% possession. Only 5 defensive line breaks conceded illustrates their defensive discipline. GHORBANI (12.5 km), REZAEIAN (11.9 km), and EZATOLAHI (11.8 km) drove the work-rate that made the draw feel like two dropped points for Egypt."
